{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5","id":1405072,"title":"Would the Gangrel & Nosferatu Elders accept Gargoyles into their numbers in V5?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-28T08:42:07-07:00","id":1405072,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Would the Gangrel & Nosferatu Elders accept Gargoyles into their numbers in V5?","content":"As the topic title states,<br /> <br /> I've always seen Gargoyles as a strange hybrid diaspora to most of their origin clans (Gangrel, Tzimisce &amp; Nosferatu) and with first light finding out, then of course 2008 attack on Vienna, it'd become important for them to disappear as much as any other Kindred, so they'd need allies and places to hide. So If they approached the Gangrel &amp; Nosferatu, would they be accepted to mingle among them, work with them and possibly become honorary clans members?<br /> <br /> As for why I specifically chose those two clans, it's because of The Montmartre Pact, which would probably be well known as the reason Free Gargoyles are left alone by Tremere (officially, but who knows behind closed doors).<br /> <br /> I am only asking because I know there's a lot of older books from V1-Revised era as well as Dark Ages that I may have missed with info on their Clans feelings on Gargoyles before V5, also possibly to go through and structural changes that stuff like the Beckoning(&lt;9 gen being gone/leaving for the middle east) and knowing the Second Inquisition is on the prowl that may make them reconsider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13247-incognito","name":"InCogNito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T10:34:10-07:00","id":1405087,"title":"","content":"on a case by case basis this was likely happening before v5. <br /> <br /> with v5... either they're being righteously bloodhunted for going postal or they remain loyal through all the Dominate, rituals and propaganda they have been suscepted too. Even though some chantries have hung up new flags they aren't going to unchain one of their best war resources.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T10:44:28-07:00","id":1405088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405087#post1405087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">on a case by case basis this was likely happening before v5.<br /> <br /> with v5... either they're being righteously bloodhunted for going postal or they remain loyal through all the Dominate, rituals and propaganda they have been suscepted too. Even though some chantries have hung up new flags they aren't going to unchain one of their best war resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more talking about the <b>*Double checks* </b>528 years of Gargoyles who were or became free before Vienna/SI and the ones that were embraced by a free gargoyles and their plans of action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13247-incognito","name":"InCogNito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T12:19:46-07:00","id":1405096,"title":"","content":"Well, you specified V5, yet you want to talk about gargoyles pre v5?<br /> <br /> As I said; a case by case basis. depends what city you're in and the power dynamic of the clans/age of the members/specific people. Sheltering a gargoyle might be a difficult political issue best avoided, the old nos might just remember fighting against the gargoyles, they might suspect a tremere plant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T16:29:26-07:00","id":1405106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405096#post1405096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you specified V5, yet you want to talk about gargoyles pre v5?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah years before the destruction of Vienna's Chantry would inform where Garagoyles as a bloodline stand and what alliances they made and played upon once they heard news that not only did Firstlight exist but ,at least for the case of the Tremere, know exactly where to strike. I was just clairify that I was talking about the free Garagoyles as that's 528 years of politics for the Gargoyles as an (overtly) free &quot;bloodline&quot; I've not heard too much. Their leadership, how they organize and their relationship with the other clans, beside Tremere, in the metaplot was only briefly touched on materials I've seen. See these are questions that involve V5 but also pre-V5 metaplot issues/information.<br /> <br /> Also<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405096#post1405096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the old nos might just remember fighting against the gargoyles, they might suspect a tremere plant...</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember almost all the 4th-9th gens are gone to the middle east, so that leaves a lot of of the bad blood in the Broods off the table in regards to Nos X remembering how gargoyle Y hurt them.<br /> <br /> I overall know it's case by case basis but was curious if people who knew more than myself had a clue on what metaplot pre-v5 may inform the direction V5 Gargoyles may take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13247-incognito","name":"InCogNito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T18:15:48-07:00","id":1405110,"title":"","content":"I think they would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-28T20:42:04-07:00","id":1405119,"title":"","content":"Well this is naturally my personal opinion but I would imagine that the Gargoyles probably do retain contacts with their original clans, even as bloodlines, to a certain extent.<br /> <br /> We know that clans Gangrel and Tzimisce still carry a massive chip on their shoulder over the creation of Gargoyles and I bet the Nosferatu are pretty testy regarding the issue as well. We know that for years the Ivory Tower has forced the practice into secrecy because rumor of Gargoyles tends to whip the Gangrel and Nosferatu into a lather pretty well.<br /> <br /> I would personally imagine that a few escaped and rescued Gargoyles probably have returned to their parent clans over the centuries, but probably not a ton given that the numbers of Independent and Anarch Gargoyles is still relatively low.<br /> <br /> While each clan is a spectrum I imagine that most Tzimisce would feel an obligation to release their kin from their suffering and avenge them more then anything else. Unless the affliction can be reversed, Gargoyles are basically cut off from the prospect of Metamorphosis and so their fates are either as servants or to be destroyed and I can easily see the pride of the fiends leading them to maintain that destruction was better and far more merciful, for the individual and the clan.<br /> <br /> I can see Gangrel welcoming back their lost kin but it would obviously be difficult as Gargoyles would still be expected to be capable of surviving on their own. I imagine the clan culture would be sympathetic to Gargoyles and Gargoyle legacies but expect them to survive by their own merit. Clan Gangrel will avenge itself upon the warlocks still, but they won't coddle the Gargoyles either. <br /> <br /> I see the Nosferatu as being the most concerned as welcoming for their lost clanmates as individuals. They're still marred and perhaps are even more cursed now and the familial ties of the Nosferatu are likely to still extend. I imagine them making niches in their warrens for Gargoyle legacies and working alongside the defectors to undermine the Tremere whenever possible. The clan may be less likely to war over honor like the other two, but they would still prefer a weak Tremere - after all, weak Tremere don't threaten their information networks or abduct Nosferatu for experimentation. So long as the Gargoyle bloodlines still fear the Nictuku, I see them being welcomed as brothers.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the appearance of Gargoyles, throughout history, has been something that always shakes up the sects and so the Pyramid must be extremely careful with them. Gargoyles breaking loose remind the Ivory Tower not only of the Tremere's self-surviving ambition and treachery; but it riles up the Gangrel and Nosferatu enough to threaten the peace of the sect. The Sabbat have a field day trying to recruit Gargoyles for war against House Tremere, to illustrate how the Camarilla cares nothing for its own, and to further radicalize its own ranks - particularly House Goratrix and the Tzimisce. The Anarch Movement has a propaganda holiday whenever a new Gargoyle reaches their ranks as they decry the tyranny of the elders and the blind eye cast by the Camarilla to the obviously on-going threat of Clan Tremere - the most despotic of clans. An Anarch Tremere in many ways becomes as valuable a propaganda piece as an Anarch Ventrue.<br /> <br /> As time has gone on though, there is naturally many questions about how the Gargoyles interacted with their kin. What roles they played in the Anarch Revolts, the Gangrel Exodus, the Vienna Incident, etc.<br /> <br /> It's a ripe territory for writers, STs, and players imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T00:52:53-07:00","id":1405138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405119#post1405119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well this is naturally my personal opinion but I would imagine that the Gargoyles probably do retain contacts with their original clans, even as bloodlines, to a certain extent.<br /> <br /> We know that clans Gangrel and Tzimisce still carry a massive chip on their shoulder over the creation of Gargoyles and I bet the Nosferatu are pretty testy regarding the issue as well. We know that for years the Ivory Tower has forced the practice into secrecy because rumor of Gargoyles tends to whip the Gangrel and Nosferatu into a lather pretty well.<br /> <br /> I would personally imagine that a few escaped and rescued Gargoyles probably have returned to their parent clans over the centuries, but probably not a ton given that the numbers of Independent and Anarch Gargoyles is still relatively low.<br /> <br /> While each clan is a spectrum I imagine that most Tzimisce would feel an obligation to release their kin from their suffering and avenge them more then anything else. Unless the affliction can be reversed, Gargoyles are basically cut off from the prospect of Metamorphosis and so their fates are either as servants or to be destroyed and I can easily see the pride of the fiends leading them to maintain that destruction was better and far more merciful, for the individual and the clan.<br /> <br /> I can see Gangrel welcoming back their lost kin but it would obviously be difficult as Gargoyles would still be expected to be capable of surviving on their own. I imagine the clan culture would be sympathetic to Gargoyles and Gargoyle legacies but expect them to survive by their own merit. Clan Gangrel will avenge itself upon the warlocks still, but they won't coddle the Gargoyles either. <br /> <br /> I see the Nosferatu as being the most concerned as welcoming for their lost clanmates as individuals. They're still marred and perhaps are even more cursed now and the familial ties of the Nosferatu are likely to still extend. I imagine them making niches in their warrens for Gargoyle legacies and working alongside the defectors to undermine the Tremere whenever possible. The clan may be less likely to war over honor like the other two, but they would still prefer a weak Tremere - after all, weak Tremere don't threaten their information networks or abduct Nosferatu for experimentation. So long as the Gargoyle bloodlines still fear the Nictuku, I see them being welcomed as brothers.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the appearance of Gargoyles, throughout history, has been something that always shakes up the sects and so the Pyramid must be extremely careful with them. Gargoyles breaking loose remind the Ivory Tower not only of the Tremere's self-surviving ambition and treachery; but it riles up the Gangrel and Nosferatu enough to threaten the peace of the sect. The Sabbat have a field day trying to recruit Gargoyles for war against House Tremere, to illustrate how the Camarilla cares nothing for its own, and to further radicalize its own ranks - particularly House Goratrix and the Tzimisce. The Anarch Movement has a propaganda holiday whenever a new Gargoyle reaches their ranks as they decry the tyranny of the elders and the blind eye cast by the Camarilla to the obviously on-going threat of Clan Tremere - the most despotic of clans. An Anarch Tremere in many ways becomes as valuable a propaganda piece as an Anarch Ventrue.<br /> <br /> As time has gone on though, there is naturally many questions about how the Gargoyles interacted with their kin. What roles they played in the Anarch Revolts, the Gangrel Exodus, the Vienna Incident, etc.<br /> <br /> It's a ripe territory for writers, STs, and players imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with your analysis 100%. The Tzimisce are a cold and proud clan, and would probably not welcome the Gargoyles as prodigal sons back into the fold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T02:09:14-07:00","id":1405143,"title":"","content":"Most Tzmisce aren't into metamorphosis all that much. They are far more pragmatic than given credit for here. That said, of the three source clans, Tzmisce have gotta be the best and worse case scenario: Gargoyles may become property and enter servitude not unlike that with the Tremere, or they might end up on the cutting board as a laboratory animal. Or alternatively you might be treated like a prized guest with no expense spared. Tzmisce are knife-edge characters. <br /> <br /> If it weren't for the potenetial political fallout/suspicion, it's always good to have a gargoyle. A Gargoyle is a pretty good asset given reputation alone. Generally I feel the rolls of primogen should in most cities extend to cover non-camarilla clans and bloodlines and individuals; nobody wants their bloodline to fall under the jurisdiction of the Tremere, and yet often they do as the political might of the clan leaves them with no serious opposition. Gargoyles, like Samedi, are quite contested. <br /> <br /> -Most low gens didn't go to the middle east in V5. Just a few of them. They've backtracked on that one pretty hard with most scenario books keeping most of their low gens. Either way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13247-incognito\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13247\" data-vbnamecard=\"13247\">InCogNito</a> , if the elders left that would've had a gargoyle grudge, wouldn't the ones that remember the history of the gargoyles and how they're all one blood also leave? <br /> That said, Nosferatu have an implied thing going on with the Samedi, and their only links are obfuscate and being ugly. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T05:09:08-07:00","id":1405151,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to say &quot;Gargoyles didn't survive the transition to V5&quot;. With the premise of the Second Inquisition and things as everyday as <i>mobile phones</i> being actively hostile to vampires, the obviously non-human Gargoyles do not fit in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T05:31:21-07:00","id":1405152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405151#post1405151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to say &quot;Gargoyles didn't survive the transition to V5&quot;. With the premise of the Second Inquisition and things as everyday as <i>mobile phones</i> being actively hostile to vampires, the obviously non-human Gargoyles do not fit in.</div> </div> </div> </div>or maybe they're immobile statues, sitting around, patiently waiting for the whole SI business to end","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T06:29:49-07:00","id":1405154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405152#post1405152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> or maybe they're immobile statues, sitting around, patiently waiting for the whole SI business to end</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point \ud83d\ude0a","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T08:54:30-07:00","id":1405170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405151#post1405151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to say &quot;Gargoyles didn't survive the transition to V5&quot;. With the premise of the Second Inquisition and things as everyday as <i>mobile phones</i> being actively hostile to vampires, the obviously non-human Gargoyles do not fit in.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In seriousness, you raise an interesting point: Do Gargoyles actually fit the paradigm of V5? They're a bloodline of deformed, dehumanized slaves engineered for subservience; Given the precedent set by thinbloods, V5, as an optimistic egalitarian setting, is either bound to make gargoyles into something they are not, or they have to get rid of them, or some combination of the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T14:30:57-07:00","id":1405200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405119#post1405119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While each clan is a spectrum I imagine that most Tzimisce would feel an obligation to release their kin from their suffering and avenge them more then anything else. Unless the affliction can be reversed, Gargoyles are basically cut off from the prospect of Metamorphosis and so their fates are either as servants or to be destroyed and I can easily see the pride of the fiends leading them to maintain that destruction was better and far more merciful, for the individual and the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tzimisce has a been overall quiet as things go compared to the other clans especially since they're now the sole &quot;dedicated&quot; clan to the Sabbat if you take the Lasombra's defection as canon to the meta plot, so it's part of the reason left them out/off the menu regarding everything I said as in the metaplot it feels like there's too many questions to be answered that their introduciton of what they're doing can fill in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405119#post1405119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can see Gangrel welcoming back their lost kin but it would obviously be difficult as Gargoyles would still be expected to be capable of surviving on their own. I imagine the clan culture would be sympathetic to Gargoyles and Gargoyle legacies but expect them to survive by their own merit. Clan Gangrel will avenge itself upon the warlocks still, but they won't coddle the Gargoyles either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which make sense, they're still a clan of 'Might makes right' in a lot of ways and as long as you're not pompus and can pull your weight you'd be considered cool to hang.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405119#post1405119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see the Nosferatu as being the most concerned as welcoming for their lost clanmates as individuals. They're still marred and perhaps are even more cursed now and the familial ties of the Nosferatu are likely to still extend. I imagine them making niches in their warrens for Gargoyle legacies and working alongside the defectors to undermine the Tremere whenever possible. The clan may be less likely to war over honor like the other two, but they would still prefer a weak Tremere - after all, weak Tremere don't threaten their information networks or abduct Nosferatu for experimentation. So long as the Gargoyle bloodlines still fear the Nictuku, I see them being welcomed as brothers.</div> </div> </div> </div>This right here is probably where i'd point out they'd most likely be an interclan cold war of information and one-upmanship, especially within the Camarilla as both have lost some ground (Nos because they lost SchreckNet and Tremere because they lost their founders &amp; the solidified structure of a clan they once had)<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405119#post1405119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As time has gone on though, there is naturally many questions about how the Gargoyles interacted with their kin. What roles they played in the Anarch Revolts, the Gangrel Exodus, the Vienna Incident, etc.<br /> <br /> It's a ripe territory for writers, STs, and players imo.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep which is why I poised the question I know a lot of it will be left up to each player to determine but there's also the metaplot/grounding. Especially with how Disciplines have been reworked so heavily, it will be interesting to see if they collapse things like their Visceratika and Flight into potentially a unique Disciplines or whatever. Also what happens regarding Thinblood-ism in embraced Gargoyles bloodlines, but that's a whole topic that is a can of worms I don't think anyone is ready to open.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405143#post1405143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-Most low gens didn't go to the middle east in V5. Just a few of them. They've backtracked on that one pretty hard with most scenario books keeping most of their low gens. Either way, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13247-incognito\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"13247\" data-vbnamecard=\"13247\">InCogNito</a> , if the elders left that would've had a gargoyle grudge, wouldn't the ones that remember the history of the gargoyles and how they're all one blood also leave?<br /> That said, Nosferatu have an implied thing going on with the Samedi, and their only links are obfuscate and being ugly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I havent been keeping up too much with the scenario books especially as they seem to be more &quot;what ifs&quot; of events with an established Canon ending metaplot (Fall of London most notably) so I wasn't aware.<br /> <br /> Yes they'd probably be cautious but with the whole shake up including the lost of SchreckNet as we know it, they may be a bit open minded to burying the hatchet especially since some gargoyles could act as good messengers as well as (for Nos standards) unorthodox scouts due to their flight and<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1405072-would-the-gangrel-nosferatu-elders-accept-gargoyles-into-their-numbers-in-v5?p=1405151#post1405151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to say &quot;Gargoyles didn't survive the transition to V5&quot;. With the premise of the Second Inquisition and things as everyday as <i>mobile phones</i> being actively hostile to vampires, the obviously non-human Gargoyles do not fit in.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is understandable as a position, I am only cautious to go with saying they were wiped out mainly because even with cellphone and all that I doubt even the SI would be willing to admit to a flying creature that appears to be made of stone exist, nor has there been any mentioned so far in V5 materials. That makes me think the Gargoyles are hiding especially after hearing about Vienna or being hidden by others (which is where my thought process is going when I asked this).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13247-incognito","name":"InCogNito","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}